                <head>DRAFT REVISION OF PARAGRAPH 5–d OF NSC
                    5429/5</head>
                <p>Should overt Communist aggression occur in the Southeast Asian treaty area,
                    invoke the UN Charter or the SEATO treaty, or both, and subject to local
                    request for assistance take necessary military and any other action to assist
                    any state or dependent territory willing to resist Communist resort to force:
                    Provided, that the taking of military action shall be subject to prior
                    submission to and approval <pb facs="0267" n="233" xml:id="pg233"/> by the
                    Congress unless the emergency is so great that immediate action is necessary to
                    save a vital interest of the United States.</p>
            </div>
